  "tail": "Batch 18 authoring is complete. The A page contains the model definition and variance theorem; the B page contains the five-assays comparison. Their item levels are 3, 4, and 5.\n\n- Carriers and evidence: [A page](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/library/statistical-models-and-experiments/biological-and-technical-replication.md), [B page](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/library/statistical-models-and-experiments/biological-and-technical-replication-examples.md), [model definition](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/items/def-biological-and-technical-replication-model.md), [theorem](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/items/thm-mean-and-variance-under-biological-and-technical-replication.md), [example](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/items/ex-five-assays-on-one-animal-versus-five-animals.md), and [batch notes](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/statistical-models-experiments-62-batch-18.notes.md).\n- I read the relevant passages in [Oehlert’s book](https://users.stat.umn.edu/~gary/book/fcdae.pdf) and [Holmes and Huber’s Chapter 13](https://www.huber.embl.de/msmb/13-chap.html). They inform the unit distinctions and limitations; the variance formulas are proved locally.\n- Checks passed: source fetch 2/2, precheck, proof layout (3 items, 10 steps), rendercheck (5 files), strict proof-contract validation, content policy, and scoped depcheck. All three Step-1 author-readiness records are `ready`; these are not independent approval.\n\n**Owner-side run blockers**\n\n- The recomputed run remains held at Step 1 for owner repair and recertification: 37/62 batches covered, no workers in flight, and batch 18 still lacks a native stage artifact. The persisted batch-dependency artifact is stale after the manifest update; an in-memory recomputation confirms batch 18 remains level 3 with suppliers 1 and 7.\n- A final manifest integrity read found malformed JSON in 